invariant: INV-55
file: handshake_post.c
catches: unit
reason: ch_read answers each request at once, so a run of requests costs
  one write-side rekey and one send inside ch_read apiece, where RFC 9846
  section 4.7.3 has one answer serve every request read while this side
  is silent. bin/unit reads a full run of requests, requires no send from
  that read and one KeyUpdate from the next write.

--- old
    if (request == 1 && t->send_epochs < HSPOST_SEND_EPOCHS_MAX) {
        t->key_update_owed = 1;
    }
--- new
    if (request == 1 && t->send_epochs < HSPOST_SEND_EPOCHS_MAX) {
        (void)hspost_send_key_update(t);
    }
